From a010cf786b688ecbd3715bf290d3ea831dfffc1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cyhhao <5381613+cyhhao@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:42:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(config): stop readers seeing a half-written config

In-process config writers rewrite config.yaml by truncating it and then
writing it, so a concurrent reader (a reload's LoadConfig, the
management config endpoints, the management stale-snapshot check, a
read-modify-write save) could see an empty or partial file. An empty
read loads as defaults: no api-keys and no management secret until the
next event reloads the full file.

Order every in-process config write against those reads with one
RWMutex (config.WriteConfigFile / config.ReadConfigFile). Writes stay in
place, keeping the inode of a mounted config file, and are fsynced. A
call-site test parks each reader and the management write inside its
file I/O on a named pipe and checks that it holds the lock there.

Upstream: router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI#6701 at 0cd78a14a.
